# L §6.4, §8.3 (GD-18; tally 2.1.6, issue #62): with every ask, the base's q_low, refused alone, prints its refusal
# in the asks' order, between q and q_raised, and the others answer. tally 2.1.5's refcore left q_low out.
=== model.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "T's base for M0's load-code fixtures (invented): a model and a scenario over it, scen.tally; it loads clean"

source card "T's fixture card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money PLN

def doubled: money PLN = amt + amt at reader

ask q: doubled law 2026-03-01

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "the card"

ask q_low: doubled in lowered law 2026-03-01
=== scen.tally
scenario raised over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version raise_2027
  cite card
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-02-01
  replace amt = 150.00 PLN "a raise from 2027"

ask q_raised: doubled in raised law 2027-06-01
=== expect
q: 200.00 PLN
  law date 2026-03-01, cut 2026-03-01
q_low: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ask q_low names lowered, neither the model nor a loaded scenario (model.tally:24)
q_raised: 300.00 PLN
  world: raised
  held: amt = 150.00 PLN (raise_2027), read for 2027-06-01
  law date 2027-06-01, cut 2026-03-01
